    LLM: 'Switch only when the combined two-hand expectation improves; do not optimize one hand while leaving the other nearly dead.\n\nTrack the cards, suits, or resources that control the next legal plays, and avoid giving opponents a simple route to their scoring condition.\n\nUse memory and tempo to force opponents into inefficient plays while preserving cards or resources that complete your own plan.',
